t":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let slice = ['l', 'o', 'r', 'e', 'm'];"},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = slice.windows(3);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['l', 'o', 'r']);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['o', 'r', 'e']);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['r', 'e', 'm']);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(iter.next().is_none());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If the slice is shorter than `size`:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let slice = ['f', 'o', 'o'];"},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = slice.windows(4);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(iter.next().is_none());"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Because the [Iterator] trait cannot represent the required lifetimes,"},{"DocComment":" there is no `windows_mut` analog to `windows`;"},{"DocComment":" `[0,1,2].windows_mut(2).collect()` would violate [the rules of references]"},{"DocComment":" (though a [LendingIterator] analog is possible). You can sometimes use"},{"DocComment":" [`Cell::as_slice_of_cells`](crate::cell::Cell::as_slice_of_cells) in"},{"DocComment":" conjunction with `windows` instead:"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [the rules of references]: https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-02-references-and-borrowing.html#the-rules-of-references"},{"DocComment":" [LendingIterator]: https://blog.rust-lang.org/2022/10/28/gats-stabilization.html"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" use std::cell::Cell;"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let mut array = ['R', 'u', 's', 't', ' ', '2', '0', '1', '5'];"},{"DocComment":" let slice = &mut array[..];"},{"DocComment":" let slice_of_cells: &[Cell<char>] = Cell::from_mut(slice).as_slice_of_cells();"},{"DocComment":" for w in slice_of_cells.windows(3) {"},{"DocComment":"     Cell::swap(&w[0], &w[2]);"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(array, ['s', 't', ' ', '2', '0', '1', '5', 'u', 'R']);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"Builtin":{"TrackCaller":{"Untagge